Nmap, Ncat and Nping
--------------------

The binaries published in this repository's releases are built from the
unmodified official Nmap source releases at https://nmap.org/dist/. Each
tarball's GPG signature is checked against the Nmap Project Signing Key
before the build.

Nmap is Copyright (c) Nmap Software LLC and its contributors, and is licensed
under the NPSL (https://nmap.org/npsl/). The Nmap Reference Guide (the man
pages) is also available under the Creative Commons Attribution License 3.0.

Each release carries the exact source code its binaries were built from:
the official Nmap source tarball with its signature, and the OpenSSL source
tarball. The scripts that control the build are in this repository, at the
release's tag.


Third-party components
----------------------

The binaries statically link the following components. Their full license
texts are in share/doc/nmap/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES in every release archive.

  Component            Obtained from          License
  OpenSSL              openssl.org            Apache-2.0
  libpcap              bundled with Nmap      BSD-3-Clause
  libdnet              bundled with Nmap      BSD-3-Clause
  PCRE2                bundled with Nmap      BSD-3-Clause WITH PCRE2-exception
  libssh2              bundled with Nmap      BSD-3-Clause
  LIBLINEAR            bundled with Nmap      BSD-3-Clause
  Lua, LPeg            bundled with Nmap      MIT
  zlib                 Alpine Linux           Zlib
  musl libc            Alpine Linux           MIT
  libgcc, libstdc++    Alpine Linux (GCC)     GPL-3.0-or-later WITH GCC-exception-3.1

Nmap's license explicitly permits linking with OpenSSL (NPSL section 11).

The licenses/ directory of this repository holds the license texts of musl,
LPeg and the GCC Runtime Library Exception. They are not part of the source
trees the build uses, so the build takes them from there.


